Third-party attributions
========================

ASHRAE equations
----------------
The psychrometric correlations implemented in src/core/psychro.js follow the
equations published in the ASHRAE Handbook — Fundamentals, Chapter 1
("Psychrometrics"), and the ASHRAE TC 9.9 thermal guideline envelope limits.
Equation numbers are cited at each implementation site. This project implements
the published mathematics; it includes no ASHRAE text or tables and is not
endorsed by ASHRAE.

CoolProp (MIT License)
----------------------
The committed reference dataset test/reference/coolprop-reference.json is
generated with CoolProp (https://coolprop.org), the open-source thermophysical
property library, via its HAPropsSI humid-air interface (ASHRAE RP-1485
formulation: Herrmann, Kretzschmar & Gatley 2009). CoolProp is used as a
development/test-time accuracy oracle only; no CoolProp code ships in the app.

  Bell, I.H., Wronski, J., Quoilin, S., Lemort, V. (2014). "Pure and
  Pseudo-pure Fluid Thermophysical Property Evaluation and the Open-Source
  Thermophysical Property Library CoolProp", Ind. Eng. Chem. Res. 53(6),
  2498–2508.

